Support DVP sensors that only expose UYVY in esp_capture 0.8.4.

ESP_CAPTURE_FMT_ID_YUV422 means YUYV to everything downstream, so a sensor that
only offers V4L2_PIX_FMT_UYVY is dropped during enumeration and negotiation ends
with "No supported format". One Mosaico CameraBoard variant carries an SC101IOT
whose 640x480 mode is UYVY only, and unlike MIPI-CSI the DVP controller performs
no byte swapping of its own.

Recognise UYVY, remember which of the two orders the device enumerated, request
that order in VIDIOC_S_FMT, and swap the 16-bit words after capture so the rest
of the pipeline still sees YUYV. Devices offering YUYV keep using it untouched.
The existing RGB565 endianness helper does exactly this swap, so it is reused
and renamed accordingly.

Normalize UYVY before optional YUV420 conversion so that both output paths
receive the YUYV order expected by the converter.

